{
  "title": "Contract-first: generating routes and mocks",
  "summary": "Let the contract drive the endpoints: one direct route per operationId, mock mode for early consumers, and fail-fast when a route is missing.",
  "minutes": 13,
  "kind": "lesson",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Contract-first versus code-first",
      "body": [
        "- **Code-first**: write the implementation, generate the OpenAPI from it afterwards. Quick for one team; the",
        "  contract ends up being whatever the code happened to do.",
        "- **Contract-first**: agree the OpenAPI with consumers **first** (or alongside), then implement it. The contract is",
        "  a reviewed artefact in Git; consumers, mocks, the gateway and tests all work from it in parallel.",
        "",
        "For an integration platform, contract-first wins: the gateway imports the contract, the developer portal shows it,",
        "and the integration is generated from it. One file, so the gateway and the integration can **never disagree**",
        "about which operations exist."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Put a contract-first delivery in order.",
      "lines": [
        "Draft the OpenAPI contract with the consuming team",
        "Review and merge it into Git",
        "Generate the REST definition from it and turn on mock mode",
        "Consumers start building against the mocks",
        "Implement one route per operationId",
        "Turn mock mode off and publish the same contract on the gateway"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "What generation gives you",
      "body": [
        "In Camel, a REST definition can point at the contract instead of listing paths:",
        "",
        "```yaml",
        "- rest:",
        "    openApi:",
        "      specification: openapi.json",
        "      missingOperation: fail      # or: mock, ignore",
        "- restConfiguration:",
        "    clientRequestValidation: true",
        "```",
        "",
        "For **every operation**, Camel creates the endpoint and forwards the request to **`direct:<operationId>`**.",
        "You write one route per operation: `from: direct:getBook`. The name must match **exactly**.",
        "",
        "- `missingOperation: mock` answers operations that have no route yet with the contract's **example**.",
        "  Consumers can start on day one.",
        "- `missingOperation: fail` (the default) refuses to **start** if any operation has no route. That is what you",
        "  want in production: no silent example answers.",
        "- `clientRequestValidation: true` rejects requests that break the contract's **required** rules (a missing",
        "  required parameter or body) with `400`. It does not check every `pattern`, so keep your own validation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Someone adds `deleteBook` to the contract but forgets the route. Mock mode is off (`missingOperation: fail`). What happens on the next deployment?",
      "options": [
        "The integration refuses to start, naming the missing operation; the problem is caught before any consumer sees it",
        "`DELETE /books/{isbn}` returns the contract example",
        "`DELETE /books/{isbn}` returns 404 forever",
        "Camel silently ignores the new operation"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Fail-fast at startup turns a production mystery into a failed deployment, which the pipeline catches."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "The contract says `isbn` has `pattern: ^97[89][0-9]{10}$`. Client request validation is on. A request arrives for `/books/abc`. Why might it still reach your route?",
      "options": [
        "Client request validation checks required parameters and bodies, not every schema rule; add a validate step for the pattern",
        "Patterns only apply to query parameters",
        "The gateway removed the pattern",
        "It cannot: Camel always enforces patterns"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Know what each layer actually checks. Assumed validation is the most dangerous kind."
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Headers or variables?",
      "body": [
        "In contract-first routes, path and query parameters arrive as **headers** (`isbn`, `q`). Before you call any",
        "backend, decide where each value should live:",
        "",
        "- **Header**: travels with the message and may be **sent by the next producer**. Only for values you *mean* to transmit.",
        "- **Variable**: stays inside the route; no component ever sends it. For everything you just need later.",
        "",
        "The standard opening of an operation route therefore is:",
        "",
        "```yaml",
        "- route:",
        "    from:",
        "      uri: direct:getBook",
        "      steps:",
        "        - setVariable: { name: isbn, simple: \"${header.isbn}\" }",
        "        - removeHeaders: { pattern: \"*\" }",
        "        - validate: { simple: \"${variable.isbn} regex '^97[89][0-9]{10}$'\" }",
        "        - toD: \"http:{{catalogue.url}}/api/books/${variable.isbn}?httpMethod=GET\"",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sort",
      "prompt": "Header or variable?",
      "buckets": [
        "Keep as a variable",
        "Send as a header"
      ],
      "items": [
        [
          "The ISBN, needed only to build the backend URL",
          0
        ],
        [
          "The customer id, used in a log line and a jq mapping",
          0
        ],
        [
          "The trace id the backend must log",
          1
        ],
        [
          "`Content-Type: application/json` for the outgoing POST",
          1
        ],
        [
          "The page number, used to compute an offset",
          0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Start up, mock, or refuse",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `string Startup(string openApiJson, ISet<string> directRoutes, string missingOperation)`:",
        "",
        "- collect every operation's `operationId` (operations are the `get`/`put`/`post`/`delete`/`patch` keys under each path);",
        "- `missing` = operationIds with no entry in `directRoutes`, sorted ordinally;",
        "- no missing routes → `\"started\"`;",
        "- `missingOperation == \"mock\"` → `\"started with mocks: \" + missing joined by \", \"`;",
        "- `\"ignore\"` → `\"started without: ...\"` (same list);",
        "- `\"fail\"` → throw `InvalidOperationException` whose message is `\"missing routes: \" + list`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Text.Json;",
        "",
        "string Startup(string openApiJson, ISet<string> directRoutes, string missingOperation)",
        "{",
        "    return \"started\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Text.Json;",
        "",
        "string Startup(string openApiJson, ISet<string> directRoutes, string missingOperation)",
        "{",
        "    var methods = new HashSet<string> { \"get\", \"put\", \"post\", \"delete\", \"patch\" };",
        "    using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(openApiJson);",
        "    var ids = new List<string>();",
        "    foreach (var path in doc.RootElement.GetProperty(\"paths\").EnumerateObject())",
        "        foreach (var op in path.Value.EnumerateObject())",
        "            if (methods.Contains(op.Name)) ids.Add(op.Value.GetProperty(\"operationId\").GetString()!);",
        "",
        "    var missing = ids.Where(id => !directRoutes.Contains(id)).OrderBy(id => id, StringComparer.Ordinal).ToList();",
        "    if (missing.Count == 0) return \"started\";",
        "    var list = string.Join(\", \", missing);",
        "    return missingOperation switch",
        "    {",
        "        \"mock\" => \"started with mocks: \" + list,",
        "        \"ignore\" => \"started without: \" + list,",
        "        _ => throw new InvalidOperationException(\"missing routes: \" + list),",
        "    };",
        "}"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Collect the ids exactly like the previous lesson, then `Where(id => !directRoutes.Contains(id))`.",
        "Names must match exactly: `getbook` is not `getBook`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "var dojoContract = \"\"\"",
        "{",
        "  \"openapi\": \"3.1.1\",",
        "  \"info\": {",
        "    \"title\": \"Catalogue API\",",
        "    \"version\": \"1.0.0\"",
        "  },",
        "  \"servers\": [",
        "    {",
        "      \"url\": \"/catalogue/v1\"",
        "    }",
        "  ],",
        "  \"paths\": {",
        "    \"/books/{isbn}\": {",
        "      \"get\": {",
        "        \"operationId\": \"getBook\",",
        "        \"parameters\": [",
        "          {",
        "            \"name\": \"isbn\",",
        "            \"in\": \"path\",",
        "            \"required\": true,",
        "            \"schema\": {",
        "              \"type\": \"string\",",
        "              \"pattern\": \"^97[89][0-9]{10}$\"",
        "            }",
        "          }",
        "        ],",
        "        \"responses\": {",
        "          \"200\": {",
        "            \"description\": \"The book\",",
        "            \"content\": {",
        "              \"application/json\": {",
        "                \"schema\": {",
        "                  \"$ref\": \"#/components/schemas/Book\"",
        "                },",
        "                \"example\": {",
        "                  \"isbn\": \"9780134757599\",",
        "                  \"title\": \"Refactoring\",",
        "                  \"price\": 44.99",
        "                }",
        "              }",
        "            }",
        "          },",
        "          \"400\": {",
